1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,688
Where is the patient?

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,132
A patient is admitted, and planned for the ward.

3
00:00:07,482 --> 00:00:08,874
Admitted? Yes.

4
00:00:09,224 --> 00:00:11,480
Still in the Emergency Department? Maybe.

5
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:13,686
Already in the ward? Maybe.

6
00:00:14,036 --> 00:00:15,700
That uncertainty is the problem.

7
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,580
The problem isn't the admission.

8
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:21,794
It's knowing where the admitted patient actually is.

9
00:00:22,994 --> 00:00:25,634
Inpatient Pharmacy needs to know one simple thing:

10
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:28,992
is the patient still in ED, or already in the ward?

11
00:00:33,242 --> 00:00:35,496
Every time the answer isn't immediately

12
00:00:35,496 --> 00:00:37,114
visible, someone has to ask.

13
00:00:38,314 --> 00:00:40,602
And Pharmacy's work depends on that answer.

14
00:00:44,514 --> 00:00:46,129
So what if the system itself could

15
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:47,506
make that transition clearer?

16
00:00:47,856 --> 00:00:49,408
Here is an initial proposal.

17
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:52,823
While the patient is still in ED, register them in

18
00:00:52,823 --> 00:00:55,214
PHIS at Kecemasan & Trauma (Admission).

19
00:00:56,414 --> 00:00:59,998
That location would mean: still at the ED admission stage.

20
00:01:00,348 --> 00:01:02,933
When the patient physically enters the ward, the

21
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:05,356
location would be updated to the actual ward.

22
00:01:06,556 --> 00:01:09,178
But this is only an initial proposal. It must be

23
00:01:09,178 --> 00:01:11,308
validated, clinically and technically —

24
00:01:11,658 --> 00:01:14,666
including whether this is the correct PHIS mechanism.

25
00:01:15,866 --> 00:01:17,914
We may already have the information.

26
00:01:18,264 --> 00:01:20,439
The question is whether PHIS can make that

27
00:01:20,439 --> 00:01:22,614
transition visible, reliably, and with the

28
00:01:22,614 --> 00:01:23,960
least additional workload.

29
00:01:24,310 --> 00:01:26,854
Validate. Test. Pilot. Standardise.

30
00:01:27,204 --> 00:01:28,836
The goal isn't to add another step.

31
00:01:29,186 --> 00:01:31,618
The goal is to make the patient's transition visible.
